  "title": "CDR features Philipp Leibfried on the CAT's collective action regime",
  "summary": "CDR highlights growing consumer openness to class actions and notes that the UK regime is maturing, with experts pointing to recent landmark cases. Burford Capital’s Philipp Leibfried comments that the Competition Appeal Tribunal's (CAT) first-ever damages award in Kent v Apple marks a true “coming of age” for the system, signaling increasing confidence in collective redress. Learn more.",
